  "statements": [
    "SemanticDocument/OperationEngine remains sole canonical owner; History and current Scene/receipt paths stay ordered and atomic.",
    "Interaction owns region session, candidate/final selection and erase commit; Render owns existing PreparedGeometryCache/EraseMaskPathCache and local exact derived-query reuse. No extra cache/document owner in SDK, platform or demo.",
    "UR2d-A preserves existing selection EvenOdd polygon, object affine inversion, visible geometry, historical-mask subtraction, narrow contact tolerance, unsupported/invalid/error rules and group/locked/text behavior. A shared erase query is not automatically a valid selection oracle.",
    "UR2d-B shortens actual synchronous Up cost through exact query reuse, query/history preparation amortization, and measured internal copy reductions. Existing prepareRecord/publication reservation -> atomic apply -> commitPrepared/observe -> derived Scene order is preserved.",
    "Accepted inputs, confirmed Move and Up/Cancel/source-lost are not dropped or coalesced away. Pure derived candidate display requests may be coalesced only within existing selection semantics with exact final Up and correct current basis; no async Up or admission changes.",
    "No workers, no mutable prepared scratch concurrency, no UR3 rendering scheduling/preview rollout, no GPU policy/AA/brush/canonical schema change, no budget increase.",
    "R3 design is a scoped engineering input; historical descriptions of already fixed UR2a/b/c are not current defects or permission to reimplement them.",
    "This is local controlled implementation and independent source review, not an official Gate/P34, release or other-platform acceptance. No commit/push requested."
  ]
